DevOps Interview Questions at PwC 

Round 1 – Core Tech & Infra Awareness (45 mins)
• Walk me through your CI/CD pipeline — what fails first under load?
• How do you design VPCs for multi-region high availability?
• StatefulSet vs Deployment — which one and why for Kafka?
• How does kube-proxy handle traffic if IPVS rules vanish?
• How do you secure GitHub Actions workflows for internal apps?
• How does the Vault agent auto-auth with Kubernetes and renew tokens?
• Migrate MySQL to Aurora with zero downtime — what’s your approach?
• Terraform: How do you isolate and roll back a broken module?
• Explain Karpenter vs Cluster Autoscaler — when and why?
• Find all zombie processes consuming >1GB RAM — bash one-liner?

Round 2 – Chaos Simulation & RCA (75 mins)
• Latency doubled after Istio rollout — metrics look clean. What now?
• You lost access to terraform.tfstate — how do you recover infra and trust?
• Kubernetes pod is in CrashLoopBackOff with intermittent success — RCA?
• S3 upload latency spikes every 5 minutes — walk me through the triage.
• Redis maxclients hit unexpectedly — what preventive design would you improve?
• Service mesh rollout caused TLS handshake failures in prod — root cause?
• How would you simulate a node-level DNS resolution failure for testing?
• Jenkins workers go stale randomly — where do you start debugging?
• How would you build a golden image for internal Docker base layers?
• App shows 200 OK, but billing is broken — where’s your observability?

Round 3 – Mindset, Pressure & Process (30 mins)
• Ever had to say “No” to leadership for the sake of reliability?
• What’s your RCA template — and how often is it used?
• What does production readiness mean to you?
• Have you ever pushed infra changes without approval? What happened?
• How do you balance velocity with architectural safety?

💡 TL;DR:
If you haven’t:
Recovered a Terraform state loss under pressure
Triaged a 200 OK bug that was bleeding revenue
Simulated a kube-dns failure during rollout
Debugged Istio + TLS in a broken mesh at midnight
